# {{module}}

A tool server for WolOS assistants, made with `wol app new {{name}} --template ai`. An assistant
starts `bin/{{name}}` and sends JSON-RPC 2.0 messages on standard input, one per line: `initialize`,
`tools/list` and `tools/call`. Answers come back on standard output; nothing else is ever written
there (messages for a person go to standard error).

- Add a tool in `src/tools.cr`: a name, one sentence that says what it does and when to use it, a
  JSON schema for its arguments, and a method that returns text. The spec in `spec/` calls the
  server with lines in memory, so every tool is tested without an assistant.
- The server can only do what this program does. To change the system, an assistant uses the
  `wolos` tools (`wol mcp`), which ask the person first; this server never runs `wol` itself.
- Register it with your assistant as a stdio server whose command is the full path of
  `bin/{{name}}`.
- `make` builds, `make spec` runs the spec, `make check` only type-checks; `wol app check` runs the
  WolOS Crystal rules over the project.
- `AGENTS.md` tells an assistant working in this folder how the project is laid out.
